From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:49:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] kernel32: Write a profile over in place.

Saving a profile wrote over the file with CREATE_ALWAYS and
FILE_ATTRIBUTE_NORMAL, which gives an existing file those attributes --
desktop.ini, hidden and system, came out a plain file -- and which a
hidden or system file refuses on Windows.  Open it instead, and cut it to
what was written.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/kernel32/profile.c b/dlls/kernel32/profile.c
index 15663b2cbe2..a97ad85ef9a 100644
--- a/dlls/kernel32/profile.c
+++ b/dlls/kernel32/profile.c
@@ -650,8 +650,10 @@ static BOOL PROFILE_FlushFile(void)
 
     if (!CurProfile->changed) return TRUE;
 
+    /* written over in place, so that an existing file keeps its attributes -- desktop.ini its hidden
+     * and system ones, which writing over it would have to ask for again */
     hFile = CreateFileW(CurProfile->filename, GENERIC_WRITE, FILE_SHARE_READ | FILE_SHARE_WRITE,
-                        NULL, CREATE_ALWAYS, FILE_ATTRIBUTE_NORMAL, NULL);
+                        NULL, OPEN_ALWAYS, FILE_ATTRIBUTE_NORMAL, NULL);
 
     if (hFile == INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE)
     {
@@ -661,6 +663,7 @@ static BOOL PROFILE_FlushFile(void)
 
     TRACE("Saving %s\n", debugstr_w(CurProfile->filename));
     PROFILE_Save( hFile, CurProfile->section, CurProfile->encoding );
+    SetEndOfFile( hFile );
     if(GetFileTime(hFile, NULL, NULL, &LastWriteTime))
        CurProfile->LastWriteTime=LastWriteTime;
     CloseHandle( hFile );
